-- Fold dictionaries: `(<>field)` signature constraints.
--
-- The constraint declares a leading "dictionary" parameter holding the fold
-- of the in-scope `field` values; the caller supplies it explicitly as a
-- `<>` collecting fold (`(<>field folder init)`), so the fold shape and
-- result type are the caller's choice. The body reads it through `^field`.
--
-- Here `logCtx` appears in TWO scopes: nested `outer.logCtx` supplies
-- `service`, the inner `logCtx` supplies `requestId`. `(<>logCtx base.unify
-- {})` merges them (innermost scope wins on conflicting keys).
with {
mylog : (<>logCtx) => Text -> IO {}
mylog (\msg -> base.println (base.show ^logCtx ++ " | " ++ msg))
}
(do
    (with {logCtx {service "shop"}} (mylog (<>logCtx base.unify {}) "single"))
    (with {outer {logCtx {service "shop"}}} (
        with {logCtx {requestId 42}} (
            mylog (<>logCtx base.unify {}) "merged"))))
